; Bird base by the Eos route [ida2020, Fig. 7.19]: the preliminary base, then
; each of the four side corners inside-reversed along the kite crease through
; .c, the open end where the raw edges meet. `map <corner> onto --mid through
; .c` has two solutions (the circle around .c through the corner meets the
; centre line twice); the outward one meets the base only at .c and creases
; nothing, so the paper-incidence filter leaves the inward one as the single
; survivor and no `toward` is needed. The kite vertices carry sqrt(2)
; coordinates, handled exactly. --ac is never creased on this route.
;
; The seven statements are Ida's steps 2-8; the finished state is her O_8
; [ida2020, Fig. 7.20(h), p. 194]. Checked against her figures in
; notes/2026-09-12-bird-base-oracle.md.

paper square

fold --bd = map .a onto .c              ; triangle
reverse --h = map .b onto .c            ; preliminary base
reverse --v = map .d onto .c

.o = free on --bd from .b at 1/2        ; apex O, the paper centre
--mid = through .c .o                   ; centre line of the base

.sr = free on --ab from .a at 1/2       ; front-right side corner: paper (1/2, 0), table (1, 1/2)
reverse map .sr onto --mid through .c

.sl = free on --da from .a at 1/2       ; front-left side corner: paper (0, 1/2), table (1/2, 1)
reverse map .sl onto --mid through .c

.br = free on --bc from .b at 1/2       ; back-right side corner: paper (1, 1/2)
reverse map .br onto --mid through .c

.bl = free on --cd from .c at 1/2       ; back-left side corner: paper (1/2, 1)
reverse map .bl onto --mid through .c

; assert steps = 7
; assert faces = 14

; the kite: apex .c, far vertex the paper centre, all four paper corners at
; the apex. The two side vertices carry sqrt(2) coordinates and have no
; rational literal to compare against.
; assert .c = (1, 1)
; assert .a = .c
; assert .b = .c
; assert .d = .c
; assert .o = (1/2, 1/2)

; the four reversed side corners land on one point of the centre line
; assert .sr = .sl
; assert .sr = .br
; assert .sr = .bl

; the spine reverses beyond O on both halves
; assert --bd is mountain
